-- title:
--   Reducedness of k ⊗_ℤ_{(ℓ)} chartAlgInf at ℓ ∤ N
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $\ell$ a prime not dividing $N$. Write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, and let $F$ denote the field `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, in which `jFull N` is the element given by the modular function $j$. The algebra `chartAlgInf N ℓ` is `chartAlg N ℓ {(jFull N)⁻¹}`, i.e. the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of $F$ whose elements are exactly those $x \in F$ that are integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of $F$ generated by $(jFull\,N)^{-1}$; thus it is the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j^{-1}]$ in $F$. Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $\ell$, equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra structure. The assertion is that the commutative ring $k \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} \mathrm{chartAlgInf}\,N\,\ell$ is reduced. Since $k$ is an arbitrary such field, this is a geometric reducedness statement for the fibre at $\ell$ of this chart, not merely reducedness of the fibre over $\mathbb{F}_\ell$ itself.
--
--   This is the reducedness of the special fibre at a prime $\ell \nmid N$ of the chart around the cusps (the $j^{-1}$-chart) of the integral model of the modular curve of level $N$ built from the full modular function field, in the style of Igusa's Kroneckerian model. It feeds into [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.isIntegrallyClosed_tensor_chartAlgInf_of_isDiscreteValuationRing`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.isIntegrallyClosed_tensor_chartAlgInf_of_isDiscreteValuationRing), and thereby into the verification that the scheme [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255), glued from the two charts, has the expected reduction properties at $\ell$.
